{"title": "Quant Super Practice — Mock #130", "duration_min": 20.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>The minimum value of some observation is 379 and range is 71, then what is the maximum value?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2339; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2344;&#2340;&#2350; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; 379 &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2360;&#2352; 71 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325;&#2340;&#2350; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["420", "450", "430", "530"], "options_hi": ["420", "450", "430", "530"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>We know that,</p><p>Max value  -  min value = Range</p><p>Max value = 71 + 379 = 450</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>We know that,</p><p>Max value  -  min value = Range</p><p>Max value = 71 + 379 = 450</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the mode of 71,71, 72, 73, 77, 80, 85, 85, 78, 79, 73, 77, 80, 77, 75, 73, 75, 79, 77, 73, 74, 75, 77, 75?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>71,71, 72, 73, 77, 80, 85, 85, 78, 79, 73, 77, 80, 77, 75, 73, 75, 79, 77, 73, 74, 75, 77, 75 &#2325;&#2366; &#2348;&#2361;&#2369;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["73", "77", "75", "79"], "options_hi": ["73", "77", "75", "79"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Frequency of term 77 is 5 and it is highest among the given terms.</p><p>So, mode of the data is 77.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Frequency of term 77 is 5 and it is highest among the given terms.</p><p>So, mode of the data is 77.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>If each observation of the data is increased by 7.55, then what is the effect on the mean?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2310;&#2306;&#2325;&#2337;&#2364;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2309;&#2357;&#2354;&#2379;&#2325;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 7.55 &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2349;&#2366;&#2357; &#2346;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["increased by 75.5", "decreased by 6.55", "decreased by 72.5", "increased by 7.55"], "options_hi": ["75.5 &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312;", "6.55 &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2350;&#2368;", "72.5 &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312;", "7.55 &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>When each observation of the data is increased by X, then mean is also increased by X.</p><p>So, mean will be increased by 7.55.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>When each observation of the data is increased by X, then mean is also increased by X.</p><p>So, mean will be increased by 7.55.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the mean (correct up to one decimal place) of the following distribution.</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">X</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">38</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">32</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">35</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">40</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">26</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">F</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">1</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">3</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">6</td><td align=\"left\" s